# __PROJECT_NAME__

TypeScript API using pangol on __RUNTIME__. Node 22.18+ is required for Node scripts; the Bun template also needs Bun.

```sh
npm install
npm test
npm run dev
```

Visit http://127.0.0.1:3000/health. `npm run check` checks all routes;
`npm run build` generates `.pangol/routes.ts` and typechecks the project.
`npm start` runs the server after a build.

The runtime watcher restarts on changes to imported files. After adding or removing route files,
restart `npm run dev` to regenerate the route table. This starter uses a server entry point
until the framework's `pangol dev/serve` commands are available.

`src/auth.ts` rejects every credential until you connect a real session provider.
The posts example uses in-memory sample data; tests supply their own auth resolver.
An authenticated owner gets a filtered response; a different user and a missing post both get 404.
The server binds to loopback on port 3000; edit `src/server.ts` to change it.
